※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4584

※ An address is a machine word or a reference.  A narrower number is not one:
※ half of an address is not a place, and widening it would be the compiler
※ deciding which half.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u32 = 4u32
    let a: &mut u32 = ⎕at(n, ⌜&mut u32⌝)
    if a⌖ = 0u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
